{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1473850-rethinking-backgrounds","id":1473850,"title":"Rethinking backgrounds.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-02-02T12:45:52-08:00","id":1473850,"title":"Rethinking backgrounds.","content":"<br /> 1 Generation is taken too often<br /> Conventional thinking currently promotes Generation and Resources above all other backgrounds; Resources is stronger than Generation, but easier to obtain and often not desirable for &quot;street level&quot; games or for characters that want to get their hands dirty and don't want to solve all their problems with money (plebeians!) . Most of the benefits of Generation come with Dots 4 and above, Thus, on tables with some level of powergaming, we have many 8th gen and 9th gen fledglings running around, which is strange considering these generations are recommended for elders and most American* cities don't have scores of 7th gen elders (I find Games are disproportionately likely to be set in the Americas, probably because messier politics makes for better Vampire games) <br /> <br /> Generation without the power to back it up should be a trap. Without a powerful mentor supporting the vampire, a neonate with low generation should be an ever more attractive tonic in the eyes of Ancillae and high generation elders who are feeling the limits of their blood. It'd be all to easy to scheme against such neonates . Rumours of an 8th generation neonate ought to attract Sabbat packs to the city. <br /> <br /> 2: Mentor probably isn't as important as it should be. <br /> Maybe I've been reading too many trashy chinese webnovels but they've really made me rethink how family and master/disciple relationships should work in Drama. As written, a Mentor in Vampire is someone who'll occasionally get you out of trouble in return for you doing services for them. V20 even goes on to cut down on the background and states that the more powerful the mentor the less care they'll give you. Perhaps anything more intimate than that would disrupt the young vs old drama VtM's got going on, but is that likely? I don't think it is. A Sire is a vampiric <i>parent. </i>A Childe is, at the very least, an investment, and protecting your Childer should, at the very least, be a matter of Face. A sire who can't protect their childer looks weak. It's very easy for a sire to foster a positive relationship with their childer, and it's very smart for a Childe to foster a positive relationship with their sire. Bad relationships exist of course, but you can simulate that by... not taking the background (and perhaps taking a few flaws) <br /> Vampires should carefully consider the might and disposition of the vampire's backing when in conflict with another vampire. If an intruder in the Domain has little-to-no backing, they can be killed no problem, it'll be a footnote in Elysium. If the intruder has a mentor that could be pose problems, It would be considered diplomatically acceptable to stake the intruder and send her home. If the Mentor is stronger? You should definitely be opening dialogue before getting physical. If the mentor is terrifying? Bend over backwards and treat them like a royal guest. (of course, your own backing is worth factoring in the equation) <br /> <br /> 3: Status as literal titles doesn't work well.<br /> 5 dots for Prince, 2 dots for sherrif? This implies some sort of universal structure that I don't think is meant to be there. <br /> Status would really work better as a level of respect in a specific kindred community. Having plenty of positive relationships, being seen as trustworthy, displaying usefulness and loyalty to the ideals of the sect, being in favour with the people who matter, being relevant at the moment. Since players are reckless by vampire standards, this should be bouncing up and down like a yoyo. Of course, people remember the things you've done wrong <br /> <br /> 4 Some backgrounds simply cost too much at character creation for what they are. <br /> Arsenal is simply &quot;resources but worse&quot; (it works when you want to be well equiped but having 3 or more resources isn't proletarian enough for you). I think Arsenal might work well if each dot costed half a dot. Alternate Identity and Fame are also annoying backgrounds where I may want AltID or feel my concept obliges me to take fame, but they're simply of significantly less value-per dot than something like resources, allies, herd or contacts. If players could get twice as many of these lesser backgrounds, they'd be more inclined to invest and diversify<br /> <br /> <br /> 5: Backgrounds above 3 should be discouraged at character creation<br /> (at least the ones that scale exponentially, like resources. lots of dots in Contacts is a great tool for STs and I wouldn't get in the way of a player who wants that) <br /> I am on the fence: a cap at 3, or increased costs for higher levels at character creation. Go fight about it I'm really interested in what people think. Maybe the first three powers cost 1, the 4th level costs 3, the 5th level costs 6. I'm just spitballing here I haven't calculated what'd be the best numbers for it, it's late.) <br /> <br /> Why?<br /> 1: It encourages more diversity and better rounded characters at character creation. If you can't put all your dots in -clearly the best choice- then you'll have to actually think through lesser options. Going wide rather than deep leads to better rounded characters at character creation<br /> 2: It gives players something to work towards.<br /> 2: Balance: the 4th and 5th dots are often gamechangers. Gen 1-3 and Resources 1-3 don't mean that much for vampires, but these backgrounds at the 4th and 5th level are stronger than high level disciplines,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-02T13:21:15-08:00","id":1473854,"title":"","content":"A while back (yeash, at least 15+ years ago now), I decided to try to simplify my Backgrounds as much as possible. Part of this was capping everything at 5, with the optional &quot;I am master of this&quot; paragon level similar to that of the original Adventure! RPG. The other was narrowing it down to just 10 backgrounds. Exactly which 10 varied slightly from game to game, but for Vampire they were:<ul><li>Allies</li> <li>Contacts</li> <li>Influence</li> <li>Resources</li> <li>Servants</li> <li>Status</li> <li>Haven</li> <li>Herd</li> <li>Patron</li> <li>Arcane Object</li> </ul>Influence is entirely one's pull among the mortal/mundane world. Status is one's general position in the city's Kindred pecking order (which may or may not come with a title). Servants are Retainers, just with the way the relationship works made more explicit. Patron is essentially Mentor but with the caveat that there is a constant expectation of quid pro quo involved. Arcane Objects are just something I tend to make use of in my games, typically unique antiques or the like which derive power from Kindred vitae or human blood. (Most of them would probably be considered cursed.) <br /> I stopped using Generation, largely because I felt it sucked a lot of mystery out of the setting, and by just using the Blood Potency set up from Requiem, it muddled the waters regarding just where vampires come from and how long they've been around. <br /> Overall, I had pretty good results from it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-02T14:53:04-08:00","id":1473864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1473850-rethinking-backgrounds#post1473850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1 Generation is taken too often</div> </div> </div> </div>In my experience, it's either taken at the highest levels, or is used to dump a few remaining leftover points into. Characters that intend to use Dominate are much more likely to take many ranks in Generation than those that don't. Physical oriented characters often don't take it, likely because those players aren't thinking of the benefits of spending blood to boost physical traits. It can be easily overlooked. But if you have one of those playing groups that min/max a lot, then yes it is taken way too often. I haven't had that problem too much in my tabletop group though. In any LARP or online game though, I always see some kind of restriction or limit imposed because so many players in those groups do want those advantages because it isn't something that can improved by XP.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1473850-rethinking-backgrounds#post1473850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2: Mentor probably isn't as important as it should be.</div> </div> </div> </div>In general I find any of the NPC dependent Backgrounds are neglected because most Players don't want to put into time coming up with good concepts for Allies, Contacts, or even Herd. Their imagination is limited to their own PC. Mentor is usually a ST/PC collaboration because players don't know enough of the chronicle setting to do it on their own, but even here they usually don't have any ideas.<br /> <br /> Most players seem to think of Background solely in the prescribed mechanical benefit described, as opposed to the possible benefit from roleplaying with a Mentor (often their Sire, but not always so). I think this is mainly a function of what the player focuses on and the STing style of the ST. Depending on the ST, it could either be incredibly useful or annoying.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1473850-rethinking-backgrounds#post1473850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3: Status as literal titles doesn't work well.<br /> 5 dots for Prince, 2 dots for sherrif? This implies some sort of universal structure that I don't think is meant to be there.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right, but the game has never meant it to be a universal structure. It is just giving examples. In the first two corebooks when they presented Gary, Modius only had Status 3 despite being a Prince, and Lucian had Status 5 despite not having any title at all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1473850-rethinking-backgrounds#post1473850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">5: Backgrounds above 3 should be discouraged at character creation</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree. It really depends on the player and character. There are lots of good (beginning player) concepts out there that would not only justify a rank of 4 or 5, but even require it.<br /> <br /> Can it be abused? Certainly, but this is best handled between ST and Player as opposed to any universal rule. I think your concerns are all valid though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1473850-rethinking-backgrounds#post1473850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2: It gives players something to work towards.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do agree this is a common mistake for many new characters, especially in any non-level based system. The Player simply creates a character with nothing to improve on, and then they complain about it. Players need to give themselves something to achieve in character, and many times that is directly related to some kind of stat on their character sheet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":". 02-03-2022, 01:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-02T16:22:58-08:00","id":1473874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1473850-rethinking-backgrounds#post1473850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1 Generation is taken too often</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. <br /> <br /> I also find that the logistics of Generation to destroy the believability of the setting. Assuming a very conservative estimate that any given vampire Embraces their first Childe around 200-250 years of unlife, you'd be running into Thinbloods before Christianity was a thing. <br /> <br /> That said, I've also found Requiem's Blood Potency costs to be extremely prohibitive. IIRC it was Current Rating x 8, which requires a hefty investment just to get to 2bp/turn, which is better spent elsewhere. <br /> <br /> I've found a happy medium is to equate dots in Generation to the lowest Clan Discipline, which has worked out fairly well so far. <br /> <br /> I agree that social backgrounds seem a bit underpowered in most games. I think this is because these aspects of the character are not fleshed out properly at character creation. Four dots in Mentor is dope, it's basically saying your Sire is a member of the Primogen? Who cares if I have to show him how to use a clamshell? I have inside access to the city's politics, and a source for learning new Disciplines! <br /> <br /> Same with Allies, Contacts, etc. Improperly defined, they are at best afterthoughts to move a plot forward. Properly fleshed out, they become story drivers and amazing NPC's.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27252-hades","name":"Hades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-02T20:57:16-08:00","id":1473888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1473850-rethinking-backgrounds#post1473850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1 Generation is taken too often</div> </div> </div> </div>Couldn't agree more. Rules as written it's an auto 5 freebies; not only is it amazingly powerful, but it can't be purchased with XP. I don't blame players for being predictable and loading up on generation... they're only responding to overwhelming incentives.<br /> <br /> I got rid of Generation entirely, using a system we developed for our MUSH in 1999 (because Generation sucked back then, too) called &quot;Sanguinis&quot; (rated on a scale of 1-12, with 1 being weak) which is similar to what Requiem later used as &quot;Blood Potency.&quot; But you can't buy it; it goes up with time or diablerie. Your default Sanguinis is 1. It's possible, with GM approval, to spend 12 Freebies on the &quot;True Childe&quot; trait, which gives you a Sanguinis of one less of your sire's at whatever time you were embraced. That still might not be that much, although because it requires collaboration with the GM it's likely that the sire won't be a Sanguinis 2 neonate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1473850-rethinking-backgrounds#post1473850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2: Mentor probably isn't as important as it should be.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a playstyle issue more than a mechanics one, but I agree with that, too. It's up to the GM to work on this and make it worthwhile.... much like social attributes, empathy rolls, etc.<br /> <br /> I actually made one of the Tremere bonuses in my game 2 free dots in Mentor<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1473850-rethinking-backgrounds#post1473850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3: Status as literal titles doesn't work well.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with Black Fox that this isn't really meant to be taken literally -- but I also agree with your point as well. My solution is to affirmatively separate Titles and Domain control into a separate trait called &quot;Station&quot;. Station is your *official* standing, while Status is your *social* standing (with the Camarilla and aligned vampires).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1473850-rethinking-backgrounds#post1473850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4 Some backgrounds simply cost too much at character creation for what they are.</div> </div> </div> </div>This once again is a matter of playstyle. Fame can actually be quite potent if the GM is feeling jiggy. If a character has Fame that's relevant to something they are trying to do, I'll just have them add their Fame score to their Charisma+Intimidation (or whatever) straight up. I don't know what Arsenal is, but it sounds stupid. Sort of like Haven.<br /> <br /> I think Identities is actually pretty fucking cool. I don't know what the RAW is on that background -- maybe it sucks like you say -- but I play it that every new Identity comes fully documented, with birth certificates, SS cards, passports, credit ratings/history, employment histories, credit lines, etc. In a modern game, that can be gold.<br /> <br /> The point is: be a ruthless GM. Rip out the crap that seems extraneous, beef up the stuff that seems too weak, and nerf the stuff that seems overpowered. I know I probably don't need to tell you that, but it is The Way and probably can't be said too many times.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1473850-rethinking-backgrounds#post1473850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">5: Backgrounds above 3 should be discouraged at character creation</div> </div> </div> </div>Completely agree. I actually carry this further and discourage ANYTHING above 3 in Chargen (except attributes and maybe one or two abilities at most). But I'm a hardass GM in Chargen. Once play starts I'm pretty lax, but I like to get off on the right foot. Character concepts need to be really well-developed, really tight, and <b>reflected on the sheet</b>. You have a 5 in Medicine? Where are the Fame dots and Medical Influence dots? How did you get to be a world-class surgeon without becoming an integral part of the medical community?<br /> <br /> In the end, though, I completely agree with your overall take that there are SEVERE problems with Backgrounds -- a lot more than you indicated (although you did not say your list was exhaustive). It's the sloppiest-put-together part of the game... like they just threw it in at the last minute because they were tired of sketching out rules and systems. <br /> <br /> But I also think that it's an opportunity The answer (at least in my case) was to completely overhaul the system. Like No One of Consequence, I ended up with 10 core backgrounds:<ul><li>Cult (a very, very flexible background that works like a discount combo of resources, henchman, and influence)</li> <li>Fame</li> <li>Herd (Super potent in my games)</li> <li>Henchmen (Disposable and REPLACEABLE sub-retainers)</li> <li>Identities (1 full identity per dot)</li> <li>Languages (straight up 2 language per dot, total fluency)</li> <li>Library (useful for rituals and occult research, which is usually at a premium in my games)</li> <li>Mentor (Again, completely agree that this needs to be put into practice with style and vigor)</li> <li>Resources (My scale is a little broader than RAW -- I sometimes feel like the game designers didn't understand how wealth works.)</li> <li>Retainers (Dots get you &quot;Retainer Points&quot; which get spent through an algorithm to generate your retainer stats)</li> </ul><br /> There are also all the status backgrounds: Status, Sabbat Esteem, Anarch Reputation, and various Clan Prestiges.<br /> <br /> Then there's four special discipline-related Backgrounds: Affinities (for Animalism), Maskings (for use with Obfuscate disguises; couple with Identities for extra goodness), Emotions (for certain Presence powers), and Rituals (for Thaumaturgy -- ONLY taken at Chargen, as it just gives some extra starting rituals).<br /> <br /> Finally, there's Influence, which is a whole separate subset of Backgrounds... 18 different spheres of Influence. In my game, Influence is much more powerful (although obviously more limited by sphere) -- it can be used for effecting changes, getting information, sending out feelers as to what other people in the sphere are up to, etc. Like Fame, it can just be straight up added to a roll where appropriate. The spheres are: Academic, Artistic, Church, Civil, Criminal, Education, Financial, Legal, Media, Medical, Military, Occult, Police, Political, Society, Street, Transportation, Union.<br /> <br /> By both focusing/narrowing Influence AND making it more powerful, I feel like I've empowered the players' autonomy a little: they KNOW more or less the sorts of things that they are capable of doing, and their influence is in the sorts of things that their character is interested in. As written, Influence is so vague and nebulous that players either try to use it for EVERYTHING or they just sort of forget it's on their sheet. It's like Hades said -- they have to be fleshed out. But you can do that in great part with MECHANICS; you don't have to have twelve-hour long preludes. You want players actively thinking of ways to use their capabilities -- you want coteries to be capable of a wide range of flexible responses to situations.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13136-legendre","name":"Legendre","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"328"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-03T06:29:24-08:00","id":1473895,"title":"","content":"The first thing I did was remove Generation as a background\u2026 instead the player attainable levels were all trade-offs (Gen 7 and lower were unmitigated power-ups without trade-offs so drinking your way up is still desirable). Gen 10 was basically the default, higher generations got more human-ish traits (more nutrition from cold/animal blood, easier blush of health, able to hold down food longer) and reduced clan weaknesses. Gen 9 got more potent clan weaknesses (ex. +/-3 instead of +/-2) and Gen 8 had that and +1 difficulty to virtue tests.<br /> <br /> The second thing was nuking Resources as a distinct background. Most people I\u2019ve played with treat it as a super background\u2026 to buy influence, to hire retainers, to buy havens, etc. So if you want to be wealthy you instead buy a mix if influence, domain/haven, retainers, etc. reflecting their particular mix of wealth. To reflect physical things like nice cars, fancy clothes, etc. I added \u201cPossessions\u201d which could be due to wealth, but might also be stolen, or \u201cborrowed\u201d via dominate, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-03T07:24:43-08:00","id":1473897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1473850-rethinking-backgrounds#post1473850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1 Generation is taken too often<br /> Conventional thinking currently promotes Generation and Resources above all other backgrounds; Resources is stronger than Generation, but easier to obtain and often not desirable for &quot;street level&quot; games or for characters that want to get their hands dirty and don't want to solve all their problems with money (plebeians!) . Most of the benefits of Generation come with Dots 4 and above, Thus, on tables with some level of powergaming, we have many 8th gen and 9th gen fledglings running around, which is strange considering these generations are recommended for elders and most American* cities don't have scores of 7th gen elders (I find Games are disproportionately likely to be set in the Americas, probably because messier politics makes for better Vampire games)<br /> <br /> Generation without the power to back it up should be a trap. Without a powerful mentor supporting the vampire, a neonate with low generation should be an ever more attractive tonic in the eyes of Ancillae and high generation elders who are feeling the limits of their blood. It'd be all to easy to scheme against such neonates . Rumours of an 8th generation neonate ought to attract Sabbat packs to the city.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whilst I certainly agree that in V20 generation was rather problematic (munchkin's choice and all that). I do find myself missing it in V5, there's only so many times players and ST's are interested in playing the 16th-12th Generations. I think whilst it'd be hard to fix in V20 (and better handled by a thorough session zero), V5's bane-severity and associated blood-potency mechanics mean you could add it back in as an option. Though I'm not entirely sure how it'd scale.<br /> <br /> 1 dot of starting character advantage dots = 3xp<br /> Increasing blood potency by 1 = new level * 10xp<br /> Minimum increase (0-1) = 10xp or 4 dots of starting advantage dots.<br /> More likely increase (1-2) = 20xp or more than your entire allocation of starting advantages.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2: Mentor probably isn't as important as it should be.<br /> Maybe I've been reading too many trashy chinese webnovels but they've really made me rethink how family and master/disciple relationships should work in Drama. As written, a Mentor in Vampire is someone who'll occasionally get you out of trouble in return for you doing services for them. V20 even goes on to cut down on the background and states that the more powerful the mentor the less care they'll give you. Perhaps anything more intimate than that would disrupt the young vs old drama VtM's got going on, but is that likely? I don't think it is. A Sire is a vampiric <i>parent. </i>A Childe is, at the very least, an investment, and protecting your Childer should, at the very least, be a matter of Face. A sire who can't protect their childer looks weak. It's very easy for a sire to foster a positive relationship with their childer, and it's very smart for a Childe to foster a positive relationship with their sire. Bad relationships exist of course, but you can simulate that by... not taking the background (and perhaps taking a few flaws)<br /> Vampires should carefully consider the might and disposition of the vampire's backing when in conflict with another vampire. If an intruder in the Domain has little-to-no backing, they can be killed no problem, it'll be a footnote in Elysium. If the intruder has a mentor that could be pose problems, It would be considered diplomatically acceptable to stake the intruder and send her home. If the Mentor is stronger? You should definitely be opening dialogue before getting physical. If the mentor is terrifying? Bend over backwards and treat them like a royal guest. (of course, your own backing is worth factoring in the equation) </div> </div> </div>I think this really depends on the style of game you're playing, not least the Sect you're in. A high politics, Camarilla game, you definitely want a good patron backing you. But if you're playing a Nomadic Sabbat game roving all around Eastern Europe? I mean being on good terms with a Bishop won't hurt, but it's not essential.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3: Status as literal titles doesn't work well.<br /> 5 dots for Prince, 2 dots for sherrif? This implies some sort of universal structure that I don't think is meant to be there.<br /> Status would really work better as a level of respect in a specific kindred community. Having plenty of positive relationships, being seen as trustworthy, displaying usefulness and loyalty to the ideals of the sect, being in favour with the people who matter, being relevant at the moment. Since players are reckless by vampire standards, this should be bouncing up and down like a yoyo. Of course, people remember the things you've done wrong<br /> <br /> 4 Some backgrounds simply cost too much at character creation for what they are.<br /> Arsenal is simply &quot;resources but worse&quot; (it works when you want to be well equiped but having 3 or more resources isn't proletarian enough for you). I think Arsenal might work well if each dot costed half a dot. Alternate Identity and Fame are also annoying backgrounds where I may want AltID or feel my concept obliges me to take fame, but they're simply of significantly less value-per dot than something like resources, allies, herd or contacts. If players could get twice as many of these lesser backgrounds, they'd be more inclined to invest and diversify </div> </div> </div>I don't see this translated one-to-one very often. Merely that to hold X title you require Y status. So to be either an Archon or Primogen is 4-status, a Prince is 5-status, etc. However, simply having 4-status doesn't necessarilly mean you're an Archon or Primogen, same for 5-status and being Prince.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 5: Backgrounds above 3 should be discouraged at character creation<br /> (at least the ones that scale exponentially, like resources. lots of dots in Contacts is a great tool for STs and I wouldn't get in the way of a player who wants that)<br /> I am on the fence: a cap at 3, or increased costs for higher levels at character creation. Go fight about it I'm really interested in what people think. Maybe the first three powers cost 1, the 4th level costs 3, the 5th level costs 6. I'm just spitballing here I haven't calculated what'd be the best numbers for it, it's late.) </div> </div> </div>I can see more of an argument in V20, in V5 I'd generally disagree solely because of some of the loresheets available that are great for starting characters. Again I see little need for hard rules, such things are better handled in a thorough session zero with the players. Asking why someone's got 5-dots in Resources and how they're justifying that and looking to make that interesting for the story is much better than just saying no.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why?<br /> 1: It encourages more diversity and better rounded characters at character creation. If you can't put all your dots in -clearly the best choice- then you'll have to actually think through lesser options. Going wide rather than deep leads to better rounded characters at character creation<br /> 2: It gives players something to work towards.<br /> 2: Balance: the 4th and 5th dots are often gamechangers. Gen 1-3 and Resources 1-3 don't mean that much for vampires, but these backgrounds at the 4th and 5th level are stronger than high level disciplines, </div> </div> </div>Valid considerations to be sure, however, they have to be balanced against:<br /> 1. Players getting to accurately fulfil their concept. If they want to play a millionaire stock-market genius or wish to be estranged from their sire that's something to be explored.<br /> 2. Limiting players to things they'll struggle to improve (because the Chronicle is short, or they simply can't in the case of Generation) only serves to limit the stories that can be told.<br /> 3. Whilst players can have more to work for if there are limits in place, you can also ensure they have goals beyond mere background dots. Sure you've got 5-dots generation and high resources, but that's not going to save your lover's soul from the Giovanni, etc, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STV Author - <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/374164/Guide-to-the-Sabbat?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=0_0_45624_0_0_0_0\" target=\"_blank\">Guide to the Sabbat</a> <br /> Current Project(s): Tales from the Fronts - A Guide to the Gehenna War","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25061-karos","name":"Karos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25061_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-03T09:14:13-08:00","id":1473900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1473850-rethinking-backgrounds#post1473850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1 Generation is taken too often<br /> ...<br /> <br /> 2: Mentor probably isn't as important as it should be.<br /> ...<br /> <br /> 3: Status as literal titles doesn't work well.<br /> ...<br /> <br /> 4 Some backgrounds simply cost too much at character creation for what they are.<br /> Arsenal is simply &quot;resources but worse&quot; ...<br /> <br /> <br /> 5: Backgrounds above 3 should be discouraged at character creation<br /> ...<br /> <br /> Why?<br /> 1: It encourages more diversity and better rounded characters at character creation. If you can't put all your dots in -clearly the best choice- then you'll have to actually think through lesser options. Going wide rather than deep leads to better rounded characters at character creation<br /> 2: It gives players something to work towards.<br /> 2: Balance: the 4th and 5th dots are often gamechangers. Gen 1-3 and Resources 1-3 don't mean that much for vampires, but these backgrounds at the 4th and 5th level are stronger than high level disciplines,</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ill have to disagree.<br /> <br /> BUT...<br /> <br /> I think STs dont balance Backgrounds with Upkeep Costs.<br /> <br /> 1. Generation. A Neonate with low Gen and no power becomes a strong puppet, or Diablerie bait. Who is gonna miss a nobody. <br /> <br /> 2. Mentor kinda suffers from Meta-Gaming. Players usually have no experience with Master-Apprentice relationships. Mentor has a LOT of RP avenues to explore as well as story hooks, people just dont think of it.<br /> <br /> 3. Status, like Generation can make you a target, requires upkeep because other youngsters will want your or similar Status and may be desperate to get it.<br /> <br /> 4. Sorta... Something very specialized like Arsenal will have unique Upkeep Costs, such as supply as global trade breaks down, digital tracking of all the things, getting caught with illegal assault weapons, etc.<br /> <br /> 5. Discouraged...but explain that if you start with Resources5, MAINTAINING that wealth will be a lot more than just hiring a Financial wizard Ghoul. Financial Managers often struggle to beat the market, ESPECIALLY NOW!(Facebook down 20% this morning)<br /> <br /> Why?<br /> 1. It actually doesnt promote diversity if you limit choice. I think you mean power gaming vs playing the part of the Character where they gain their power base. Its more a matter of where they want to start. <br /> 2. Again, Backgrounds have constant costs(unless the ST ignores them and Player accepts them as 'granted'.) and are GREAT story hooks. (Resource4/5)Why am i being shorted on several of my startup positions and why are they all having BAD LUCK??? Is someone trying to sabotage me? Also, Resources at that level are usually tied up in investments for Tax purposes. You cash out too often, you take a Tax haircut. (Generation5)Why do i get the cold shoulder so much? Who jumped me and fed on me in that back alley...will they be back?!?!?! (Status3) Local Nosferatu told me my position was promised to some other neonates that did some work and now they are upset. One of them may go after my Ghoul.<br /> 3. Game changers? Only if you let them be. Players pick them to either live a certain Power Fantasy or RP a certain set of conditions for good or ill. Its up to the ST to make them interesting and not just the usually bemoaned 'i win' buttons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25883-inspectorg","name":"InspectorG","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-03T10:48:56-08:00","id":1473907,"title":"","content":"I know one ST that did not allow players to buy Generation. Instead, they rolled on a d10 randomly to determine it, with the worst generations more likely to come up (something like rolling 1-3 = 13th, 4-5 = 12th, 6-7 = 11th, 8 = 10th, 9 = 9th, 10 = 8th).<br /> <br /> As players it was one of those things we weren't happy about during character creation, quickly accepted during play, later discussed the merits of it... and then completely never used when we played or ran in any other game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-03T11:08:12-08:00","id":1473911,"title":"","content":"V5 backgrounds are a can of worms and If I went into it I'd start frothing at the mouth (Why does 1 dot of retainer buy pure trash? Is it because backgrounds in V5 are permanent with XP expenditure needed? So If I get a 5 dot retainer I can abuse him and send him to his death and expect an equally elite replacement by the end of the story?) <br /> <br /> <br /> But main thing:<br /> I strongly believe Generation shouldn't have tradeoffs (beyond, y'know, making you an attractive target). 10th gen is objectively better than 11th gen. 7th gen should be objectively better than 8th gen. From a moral standpoint, the reward of not commiting diablerie should be not being a murderer, getting a permanent mechanical advantage over a diablerist changes the motivation from &quot;not being a murderer&quot; to &quot;not being burdened by a whole load of physical problems&quot; which does a lot to reduce any sort of moral quandary. From a literary standpoint &quot;killing for power is bad and you should be happy with the lot you are given in life&quot; is a terrible message for satire, especially when the consequences don't have a real world parallel. On a theological basis, the hypothetical 1st gen is close to god/perfection and the dilution of the blood plays heavily into gnostic ideas of emanations and Hermetic ideas about transforming lead into gold. <br /> <br /> Letting players take 5 dots in generation is a trap, Not only is it imbalanced, it also lets them skip much of the moral struggle players should face. I've fallen into this trap. I thought &quot;If I have gen 8 I'll only need to diablerize once to get to gen 7 where I can move beyond earthly limitations and get those transcendant 6th dots (Or as I considered it before getting into esoteric ideas: Custom powers! Multiple disciplines at the same level!) <br /> First, that's not much of a struggle. One strategic murder and I'm done? Cheap. Both from a political point of view and a moral one. (getting to 6th gen or lower isn't really that viable or necessary in most games that stay within the confines of &quot;neonate&quot; or even Ancillae) An 8th gen would-be-diablerist needs to be too descriminate, since most of their peers have weaker blood that would be wasted on them (getting permanent disciplines for diablerizing higher gen vampires is fucking whack on balance) while a 12th gen vampire is going to plunge themselves into chaos in their efforts to gain strength, a far more interesting process. An 8th gen is simply finds a bound and staked vampire less tempting, and you lose conflict and drama out of that. <br /> <br /> While some people might be well meaning when they make Generation a thing of tradeoffs, they're actually encouraging conservative morality. I really hate the attitude of &quot;you were embraced 13th gen, you're stuck with it, you've got some advantages out of this: You should be happy with what you've got; trying to change that is worse than murder&quot;. The mobility of power and the struggle is what makes vampire so interesting. V5's &quot;blood potency is cancer so the lower the better&quot; really cements a conservative attitude, especially since you can get discipline dots so diablerie becomes a quick'n dirty shortcut to power rather than power in of itself ( This attitude is moreso conservative because there's also no way to weaken your blood beyond novelties beyond sanguinius: you can make the blood stronger, you can't make it weaker) <br /> <br /> <br /> All this said: 3 dots should really be the normal cap for starting neonate characters. A 4th or 5th dot should have a plot device, an accompanying flaw you get no points for: someone covets your blood and you've got at least one enemy who wants to eat you that you do not know about. <br /> <br /> <br /> RE: resource management. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25883-inspectorg\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25883\" data-vbnamecard=\"25883\">InspectorG</a> <br /> \u200bRealistically it'd be pretty easy to keep your resources up. Own a company or become a landlord, or own a patent or application and collect royalties. Money makes more money. The only serious problem vampires face is that they're dead and mostly need to hold onto their wealth through proxies who can die or get poached.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-03T12:15:20-08:00","id":1473915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1473850-rethinking-backgrounds?p=1473911#post1473911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> RE: resource management. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25883-inspectorg\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25883\" data-vbnamecard=\"25883\">InspectorG</a><br /> \u200bRealistically it'd be pretty easy to keep your resources up. Own a company or become a landlord, or own a patent or application and collect royalties. Money makes more money. The only serious problem vampires face is that they're dead and mostly need to hold onto their wealth through proxies who can die or get poached.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>FAR EASIER SAID THAN DONE.</i><br /> <br /> Resource5 isnt some Handwavium that makes reality go away. Unless the ST treats it that way.<br /> <br /> This usually is just a symptom of ignorance about the Financial System, Investing, Speculating, Interest Rates, Inflation, etc, etc...<br /> <br /> If its so easy to make money make more money, why does this happen and no one sees it coming:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=azk4DciTzng\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=azk4DciTzng\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=azk4DciTzng\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=azk4DciTzng </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Facebook/Meta losses yesterday and now<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gEpFAQ6UdNo\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gEpFAQ6UdNo\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gEpFAQ6UdNo </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gEpFAQ6UdNo\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gEpFAQ6UdNo </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Cathie Wood will jusy make that money back, yes?<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HxUzurKr-vk\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HxUzurKr-vk\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HxUzurKr-vk\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HxUzurKr-vk </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> PayPal loses $50 BILLION<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LVxB_bNk_BU&amp;t=8s\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LVxB_bNk_BU&amp;t=8s\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LVxB_bNk_BU&amp;t=8s </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LVxB_bNk_BU&amp;t=8s\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LVxB_bNk_BU&amp;t=8s </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> China looks to be having a 2008 Real Estate crash...if they are lucky<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=paFIrBDjL1c\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=paFIrBDjL1c\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=paFIrBDjL1c </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=paFIrBDjL1c\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=paFIrBDjL1c </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Globalism is dead, Supply Structures are falling apart, shortages on food and inputs for the global economy are stretched thin, yet Commodities arent even spoken about<b></b>:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4IaoZTf_NOc\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4IaoZTf_NOc\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4IaoZTf_NOc </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4IaoZTf_NOc\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4IaoZTf_NOc </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cV3QPBI8Y_s\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cV3QPBI8Y_s\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cV3QPBI8Y_s </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cV3QPBI8Y_s\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cV3QPBI8Y_s </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Why are there even Contrarian Investors if Money automatically makes more Money? <br /> <br /> Is there infinite space out, way out on the Risk Curve as well as infinite growth that paces FASTER than the 'money that gets more money'?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25883-inspectorg","name":"InspectorG","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-03T14:54:44-08:00","id":1473934,"title":"","content":"The tricky thing about generation is that it's hard to raise even if you're Sabbat and borderline impossible in carmarilla not to mention it batters your humanity. This incentives purchase of at least 1 dot at creation since 1 dot let's you make full blooded vampires.<br /> <br /> As a side a gm I know expects a justification for 4-5 dots in gen as in &quot;okay whoever embraced you is a big boy so I'm expecting sire/social based flaws.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 02-03-2022, 05:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-04T03:24:20-08:00","id":1473957,"title":"","content":"Personally I would say that a player who wants 4-5 Dots in a Background has to do some extra work to fit it in to the campaign.<br /> <br /> e.g.<br /> <br /> My Resources 5 character spent a lot of time running their business. I worked out a daily schedule, a list of offices and assets, bought a couple of contacts to cover important people in the organisation, etc, etc.<br /> <br /> A low generation character should have a sire fully generated and worked into the campaign background, plus invest some points in Mentor, Domain, Influence, etc.<br /> <br /> A high status character really needs a lot of supporting backgrounds or they will be quickly ousted","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-05T10:44:54-08:00","id":1474043,"title":"","content":"The main issue with backgrounds is that they are too abstract for many types of games, see any discussion regarding Resources.<br /> <br /> I think the simplest way to make Backgrounds more functional is to take a page from the design of 2nd edition Exalted and its Manse background. In the core book you have the basic background which gives you a magical building that generates a hearthstone, the stone gives you a magical benefit and helps restores motes (a refilling blood pack in V:tM terms). If that is all you want a Manse to be, then you can play it as such.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, a book was released that greatly expanded the meaning of the background. You still use the core book system to buy a Manse background at 1 to 5 points in value, but you then had a point buy system to build a custom manse where every dot in manse gave you two points to buy characteristics for the manse.<br /> <br /> The same sort of system applied to V:tM backgrounds would give an optional system for people who want more complexity if they desire it, but it wouldn't negate the core book background system for those that prefer simplicity.<br /> <br /> This would work well for Backgrounds like Allies, Alternate Identity, Contacts, Domain, Fame, Herd, Influence, Mentor, Resources, Retainers, and Status. But it wouldn't work as well for Black Hand Membership, Generation, or Rituals.<br /> <br /> The main issue with doing this sort of expansion is that it breaks the Background Pooling function. But when you really look into how Pooling Backgrounds work, it becomes apparent that it was intended to be a way for starter characters to have cooler things and falls apart with late game builds or characters who went ham on backgrounds at character generation. So a revised pooling backgrounds mechanic is kind of needed as is, regardless if you add the expanded point buy system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-07T09:46:18-08:00","id":1474131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1473850-rethinking-backgrounds?p=1473911#post1473911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">V5 backgrounds are a can of worms and If I went into it I'd start frothing at the mouth (Why does 1 dot of retainer buy pure trash? Is it because backgrounds in V5 are permanent with XP expenditure needed? So If I get a 5 dot retainer I can abuse him and send him to his death and expect an equally elite replacement by the end of the story?)</div> </div> </div> </div>In no small part, I think it's meant to reflect that more street-level tone V5 is designed for. 1-dot retainer is the equivalent of a fawning lover or flunkie, the sort of person a fresh embrace could get under their thumb as a minion. 2-dot/3-dot retainers are where really powerful options come in, ghouls, people with trained skills, etc. Note also V5 retainer caps out at 3-dots and a 3-dot retainer likely has mystical abilities and the stats of a gifted mortal that can eclipse many player characters. (This changes a bit if you add extra from the V5 companion but not massively. Additionally retainers have their own stock of dots based on their level.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But main thing:<br /> I strongly believe Generation shouldn't have tradeoffs (beyond, y'know, making you an attractive target). 10th gen is objectively better than 11th gen. 7th gen should be objectively better than 8th gen.<br /> <br /> <b>[...]</b><br /> <br /> While some people might be well meaning when they make Generation a thing of tradeoffs, they're actually encouraging conservative morality. I really hate the attitude of &quot;you were embraced 13th gen, you're stuck with it, you've got some advantages out of this: You should be happy with what you've got; trying to change that is worse than murder&quot;. The mobility of power and the struggle is what makes vampire so interesting. V5's &quot;blood potency is cancer so the lower the better&quot; really cements a conservative attitude, especially since you can get discipline dots so diablerie becomes a quick'n dirty shortcut to power rather than power in of itself ( This attitude is moreso conservative because there's also no way to weaken your blood beyond novelties beyond sanguinius: you can make the blood stronger, you can't make it weaker) </div> </div> </div>I think on the whole having a lower generation and higher blood potency is still stronger than not. Someone with blood-potency 3 of the 10th Generation still has an edge against someone of Blood Potency 0 of the 16th Generation. They do face some difficulties now with bane-severity and feeding restrictions, but that's meant to play into the dualism of age vs youth. The younger Cainites have less mystical power but fewer mystical weaknesses; the younger generation have more technological power/modern knowledge but also greater vulnerability because of it. (The SI is important in framing this conflict.)<br /> <br /> Also the notion that <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You should be happy with what you've got; trying to change that is worse than murder </div> </div> </div> is actively challenged in the game. Yes you will suffer humanity loss for stealing power, yes higher blood potency isn't solely an upside these days, but you absolutely can build characters focussed on seizing power through diablerie. Agata Starek is a character created for the Anarchs to do just that. She's all about literally eating the rich.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> From a moral standpoint, the reward of not commiting diablerie should be not being a murderer, getting a permanent mechanical advantage over a diablerist changes the motivation from &quot;not being a murderer&quot; to &quot;not being burdened by a whole load of physical problems&quot; which does a lot to reduce any sort of moral quandary. </div> </div> </div>I'd argue it adds more of a quandry, the question becomes what are you willing to sacrifice from power? You lose certain things by being a diablerist but gain others, the question is which is more important to you?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Letting players take 5 dots in generation is a trap, Not only is it imbalanced, it also lets them skip much of the moral struggle players should face. [...] One strategic murder and I'm done? Cheap. Both from a political point of view and a moral one. (getting to 6th gen or lower isn't really that viable or necessary in most games that stay within the confines of &quot;neonate&quot; or even Ancillae) An 8th gen would-be-diablerist needs to be too descriminate, since most of their peers have weaker blood that would be wasted on them (getting permanent disciplines for diablerizing higher gen vampires is fucking whack on balance) while a 12th gen vampire is going to plunge themselves into chaos in their efforts to gain strength, a far more interesting process. </div> </div> </div>I don't disagree that as presented in V20 generation is broken, it is <b>the</b> discipline to take at character creation in many cases. However, I think a middle-ground is ideal. While yes it can be fun to play the slow descent through the generations, exploring that struggle, etc. Eventually, players will get bored of that and want to start with a lower generation in order to tell different stories. It's hard to justify running an: Alastor, Prince, Baron, etc whose weak blood means they can't stand up effectively to their rivals, which ideally is where generation should be used.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STV Author - <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/374164/Guide-to-the-Sabbat?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=0_0_45624_0_0_0_0\" target=\"_blank\">Guide to the Sabbat</a> <br /> Current Project(s): Tales from the Fronts - A Guide to the Gehenna War","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25061-karos","name":"Karos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25061_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-07T10:59:58-08:00","id":1474134,"title":"","content":"I'm really refering to ordinary games where players start as Neonates IE the default assumption. If you want to play Ancillae+ games, ease the restrictions. <br /> <br /> <br /> (also, in V20, having lots of 5s is often stronger than having less 6's or 7s, though things fall apart at 8's and 9) <br /> <br /> <br /> IIRC Retainers in V5 (or was this just allies) had a stat for power and a different stat for reliability, making them horrendous investments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-07T11:29:16-08:00","id":1474137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1473850-rethinking-backgrounds?p=1474134#post1474134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> IIRC Retainers in V5 (or was this just allies) had a stat for power and a different stat for reliability, making them horrendous investments.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only allies have it, and it is the least well designed background in V5.<br /> <br /> But reliability is generally ignored by all the tables and even Loresheets don't seem to use it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend","name":"SetiteFriend","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-08T14:49:54-08:00","id":1474230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1473850-rethinking-backgrounds?p=1474043#post1474043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You still use the core book system to buy a Manse background at 1 to 5 points in value, but you then had a point buy system to build a custom manse where every dot in manse gave you two points to buy characteristics for the manse.<br /> <br /> The same sort of system applied to V:tM backgrounds would give an optional system for people who want more complexity if they desire it, but it wouldn't negate the core book background system for those that prefer simplicity.<br /> <br /> This would work well for Backgrounds like Allies, Alternate Identity, Contacts, Domain, Fame, Herd, Influence, Mentor, Resources, Retainers....</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes! Retainers!<br /> <br /> Like so:<br /> <br /> RETAINER POINTS:<br /> <br /> * 7 points, 1 Retainer max<br /> ** +10 points (17 total), 2 Retainers max<br /> *** +12 points, 3 retainers max<br /> **** +21 points, 5 retainers max<br /> ***** +28 points, 8 retainers max<br /> ****** +36 points, 12 retainers max<br /> ******* +46 points (160 points total), 16 retainers max.<br /> <br /> RETAINER PACKAGES: (Purchase <b><i>in order</i></b> for each Retainer, multiple purchases are possible for increased price as shown (X/Y/Z))<br /> <br /> <b>1. Basic Retainer Package: </b>1 RP<br /> You now have 1 more retainer. Your retainer has a Willpower of 2, a Humanity of 8, and 23 dots in attributes total (they do not get the free initial dot). <br /> <b>NOTE: I run a 12-attribute game. 23 dots isn't as much as it sounds like.</b><br /> \u00b7 Only two attributes can be at 3;<br /> \u00b7 No attribute can be over 3.<br /> Select any five abilities and put one dot in each of those five abilities. Then select one ability with no dots and put two dots in it.<br /> <br /> <b>2. Attribute Package: 3/5/7 RP</b><br /> \u00b7 Add 2 dots in attributes;<br /> \u00b7 No attribute can be set over 4 with this.<br /> <br /> <b>3. Willpower Boost: 4/4 RP</b><br /> \u00b7 Add 1 Willpower point.<br /> <br /> <b>4. Gifted Retainer: 4/5/7 RP</b><br /> \u00b7 Add a single dot to an attribute; that attribute may be set up to 4.<br /> <br /> <b>5. Combat Package: 3/5/7 RP</b><br /> \u00b7 Add 2 dots in combat skills;<br /> \u00b7 No ability may be set over 3<br /> <br /> <b>6. Gifted Combatant: 4/7/12 RP</b><br /> \u00b7 Give your retainer a 4th dot in any one combat skill;<br /> \u00b7 Requires that the ability be already at 3.<br /> <br /> <b>7. Supreme Combatant: 16 RP</b><br /> \u00b7 Give your retainer a 5th dot in a combat skill;<br /> \u00b7 Requires that the ability be already at 4.<br /> <br /> <b>8. General Abilities: 2/4/6/8 RP</b><br /> \u00b7 Add 4 dots in non-combat abilities<br /> \u00b7 No ability may be set over 3.<br /> <br /> <b>9. Specialty Package: 3 RP</b><br /> \u00b7 Pick two related non-combat abilities (i.e., Drive/Repair, Empathy/Animal Ken, Occult/Linguistics, Computer/Finance, Law/Finance, etc.) and give the retainer two dots in each of them. <br /> \u00b7 This package may not raise an ability above 4.<br /> <br /> <b>10. Specialization: 2/4/6/8 RP</b><br /> \u00b7 Add a 4th or 5th dot to a non-combat ability.<br /> <br /> <b>11. Ghoul Package: Free!</b><br /> \u00b7 Add a dot of Potence (and Fortitude if Gangrel);<br /> \u00b7 -1 Willpower<br /> \u00b7 Prepare to have to feed your retainer on a regular basis.<br /> <br /> <b>12. Experienced Ghoul: 6 RP</b><br /> \u00b7 Requires Ghoul Package<br /> \u00b7 +1 Vampire Lore and +1 Tremere Lore if the vampire is a Tremere.<br /> \u00b7 +1 Willpower and -1 Humanity<br /> \u00b7 You may spend 12 xp on the ghoul<br /> <br /> <b>13. Treasured Servant: 16 RP</b><br /> \u00b7 Requires: Experienced Ghoul Package<br /> \u00b7 +1 Potence (and +1 Fortitude if Gangrel)<br /> \u00b7 +1 Vampire Lore<br /> \u00b7 +1 Willpower and -1 Humanity<br /> \u00b7 The ghoul will have Status equal to your status minus two<br /> \u00b7 You may spend more 15 xp on the ghoul.<br /> \u00b7 Your ghoul receives 1/2 as much XP as you do during the course of play.<br /> \u00b7 Your ghoul will have a personality and must be RPed; he/she may be a pain in the ass sometimes.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13136-legendre","name":"Legendre","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"328"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-08T20:19:52-08:00","id":1474248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Legendre</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1473850-rethinking-backgrounds?p=1474230#post1474230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes! Retainers!<br /> <br /> Like so:<br /> <br /> RETAINER POINTS:<br /> <br /> * 7 points, 1 Retainer max<br /> ** +10 points (17 total), 2 Retainers max<br /> *** +12 points, 3 retainers max<br /> **** +21 points, 5 retainers max<br /> ***** +28 points, 8 retainers max<br /> ****** +36 points, 12 retainers max<br /> ******* +46 points (160 points total), 16 retainers max.<br /> <br /> RETAINER PACKAGES: (Purchase <b><i>in order</i></b> for each Retainer, multiple purchases are possible for increased price as shown (X/Y/Z))</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it would work better with fewer points (like 2 or 3 per background dot) and less defined packages.<br /> <br /> I would say a &quot;specialist&quot; costs more points, but I wouldn't differentiate between the types. A combat build is useless in social situations and a social build is generally useless once the napalm gets deployed. Yes this means you cheese some aspects but that is where the ST can veto the concept.<br /> <br /> Also, if a Retainer is a ghoul or not shouldn't enter into it because at any time the PC could just ghoul the Retainer.<br /> <br /> So with a point buy system you could have a large group of average people cost the same as one super retainer. A Tremere PC with several dots in Retainer to have a loyalist Gargoyle bodyguard can do a lot of damage, but on the other hand a Ventrue or Giovanni with a dozen or more financial specialist who just spend all their time improving the vampires holdings and financial power can cripple small countries, but they are useless in a fire fight.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, a Tremere or Nosferatu with max retainers as a hacking group is frightening both because of the damage they can cause and because having the Retainers spread across the world means they are very difficult to target or counter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-08T22:27:46-08:00","id":1474257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1473850-rethinking-backgrounds?p=1474248#post1474248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, if a Retainer is a ghoul or not shouldn't enter into it because at any time the PC could just ghoul the Retainer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well yes, that's why it's <i><b>free</b></i>. But it's also (I would hope obviously) a prerequisite to buying the Experienced Ghoul package and Treasured Servant package.<br /> <br /> But good call on increasing the cost of Specialist. Very good call.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13136-legendre","name":"Legendre","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"328"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-09T02:25:31-08:00","id":1474271,"title":"","content":"I run help like thus:<br /> <br /> Herd/Mob/Cult/Gang/Cult or whatever will have at most 4 dice if you want to use them for anything. It's more likely they'll have less.<br /> <br /> A 1 dot retainer will give you somebody with 5- 6 dice in a narrow role (fighting, finance, criminal doings etc) or 4 dice in many things. A 2 dot retainer will give you around 6 dice in many things or 7-8 dice in something specific. A three dot retainer could give you someone with 9/10 dice in something specific and 5-6 dice in a few other areas, or it could give you a 2 dot retainer with an added supernatural ability (a mortal thaumaturge or necromancer most likely)<br /> <br /> <br /> You can use resources to acquire help. Their pay is roughly determined by the level of their desired skill (some fields may differ more)<br /> 1 dot- 3-4 dice<br /> 2 dot- 5-6 dice<br /> 3 dot- 7-8 dice<br /> 4 dot- 9+ dice (they'll likely have fame too)<br /> <br /> You can calculate how many people you can pay by multiplying each dot of resources by the last: 1,2,6,24, 120 and so on.<br /> <br /> Though it may seem Resources is just a better investment than retainers at character creation (at higher levels at least) Retainers bought at character creation have several advantages over help acquired through resources or obtained later<br /> -They're accustomed to the peculiarities of your schedule and mannerisms.<br /> -They don't have other commitments, and will break the law if you desire it.<br /> -They're relatively stable if you've blood bound them.<br /> -They're loyal, even if you don't blood bond them (though they will need some compensation; money, status, sex, you keep their cancer riddled child alive.. etc )<br /> -If you've picked an animal retainer, they start intelligent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 02-09-2022, 12:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-09T02:36:52-08:00","id":1474272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1473850-rethinking-backgrounds?p=1474271#post1474271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though it may seem Resources is just a better investment than retainers at character creation (at higher levels at least) Retainers bought at character creation have several advantages over help acquired through resources or obtained later<br /> -They're accustomed to the peculiarities of your schedule and mannerisms.<br /> -They don't have other commitments, and will break the law if you desire it.<br /> -They're relatively stable if you've blood bound them.<br /> -They're loyal, even if you don't blood bond them (though they will need some compensation; money, status, sex, you keep their cancer riddled child alive.. etc )<br /> -If you've picked an animal retainer, they start intelligent.</div> </div> </div> </div>And, I think more importantly, Retainers are immediately available. Resources can get you suitable help in maybe a week. Retainers will be on your doorstep in an hour at most.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby","name":"James_Willoughby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar317_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-13T01:17:45-08:00","id":1474554,"title":"","content":"I rewrited most of backgrounds for my game. for resource i gave exact numbering for money(including cash, bank and assists) with money being rather low till 3 points of background which was the limit at character creation. i also did limit most of other backgrounds but not necessarily at 3.<br /> <br /> For mentor(and this is what i like most) dots represent how your relation is with your mentor rather than showing how powerful he is. at one point he might be rather distant and sometimes answer your calls while at five point you have a very close relationship.<br /> <br /> I didn't really like how mentor background worked in V20 so i came up with this instead. i agree with what it was stated regarding status, i don't use it myself because of this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27304-burnforme","name":"burnforme","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}